																		Author Notes
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608367878" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1407904169 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Aug 2014 04:29</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2087681">
									

<p>Many thanks to LongWayHome and Palaios in the forums, and djkaktus, ihpkmn, Tuomey, Zolgamax, and Mastersarge in chat for reading this over!</p>
<p>This is a rewrite of <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-943501/window-to-another-world">Window to Another World</a>, by Dax_Symbiont. Permission for the rewrite was given on the mainsite, when the original was submitted and later being voted on for deletion.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Potential&nbsp;spoilers</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">SPOILERS</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I really liked Dax’s original idea of a pane of glass that effectively let someone’s mind travel to someone else’s and take it over, essentially stealing someone’s life. I thought it over a few nights and it occurred to me, what with all the potential parallel universes out there, how many alternate versions of ourselves are living it up? Maybe they made just a few different choices, maybe they’re not ridiculously more happy, but chances are good there are a bunch of other “you”s out there who <em>are</em> happier.</p>
<p>So what’s the harm in living “your” life? Giving yourself another chance? Getting ahead of the game and dropping yourself into a place where you <em>did</em> make all the right choices, or at least most of them? Whoever created this skip (and the other prototypes) probably had these questions in mind. Question is though… are the others really “you”? What are “you” entitled to?</p>
<p>The end note, with the empty stretcher? Not everyone is totally fine with the switch, as can be expected. Nearly all of the “better-off” versions don’t make it to the other side when the switch happens, but some do.</p>
</div>
</div>
